	affiliations = {Shanghai University of Electric Power, Shanghai, China},
	abstract = {With the reduction in FPGA technology nodes and sizes, multiple bit upset (MBU) have gradually become a major reliability issue for FPGA memories in radiation environments. Strengthening memory cells is one of the important approaches to improving chip reliability. Traditional single-bit error detection and correction methods cannot provide protection against MBU faults occurring in FPGA memories, leading to storage failures and ultimately resulting in functional failures of the FPGA. In order to mitigate the impact of MBU, an interleaved Hamming code encoding protection system is designed to provide fault-tolerant protection for FPGA block memories, enabling the correction of multiple bit flip errors. The interleaved Hamming code system exhibits significant advantages over the traditional Triple Modular Redundancy (TMR) mode in terms of resource utilization and reliability. © 2024 Elsevier B.V., All rights reserved.},
